riscv32 zkVM: handler calls that do not return, field addresses, stack layout of 8-byte-aligned structs, array sizes

A call that does not return is made as a jump after the epilog only when the callee does not take
its arguments in s1-s8 while the caller restores them (JitZkHandlerConv), as fgCanFastTailCall
already decides for the other tail calls.

The alignment known for the address of a local counts the offset of a field of a struct local.

ilp32: a struct with an 8-byte-aligned field that is passed wholly on the stack is aligned to 8
bytes, as a 2*XLEN scalar is.

The slow path of the array allocation adds the elements to the base size before rounding, as the
fast path does.

Regression test: bflat-ts:calls/handler_noreturn_calls, bflat-ts:alignment/struct_values_unaligned, bflat-ts:memory/rv32_arrays_blocks

